{"id": "EUVD-2026-96616", "enisaUuid": "6689ad87-2d23-304d-99ae-d0640402c49d", "description": "JeecgBoot through 3.9.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability in GET /sys/api/getUserByName that allows low-privileged authenticated users to retrieve any user's stored password value. Attackers can decrypt the AES-CBC protected response using the hard-coded key exposed by /sys/getEncryptedString to obtain administrators' password ciphertexts for offline guessing.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T21:49:57", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T11:53:07", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AnkesKasty/cve-request-poc/blob/a7b6d1423555812d8efa26c91c5d0683164b31e5/JeecgBoot/poc_sys_api_credential_family.py", "https://github.com/jeecgboot/JeecgBoot/blob/e3b9dc0aefe1943d9772b026f64ed671a7c82802/jeecg-boot/jeecg-module-system/jeecg-system-biz/src/main/java/org/jeecg/modules/api/controller/SystemApiController.java#L100-L110", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/jeecgboot-through-3.9.5-missing-authorization-via-sys-api-getuserbyname"], "aliases": ["GHSA-ghh4-x4m2-g9rc", "CVE-2026-108677"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.23, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "c57f4488-77f1-3e2c-9303-f054a4af591e", "product": {"name": "JeecgBoot", "vendor": {"name": "n/a"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.9.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a73c5039-d181-30a2-888d-df4a2dc27a7a", "vendor": {"name": "jeecgboot"}}], "isExploited": false}